<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<page xmlns="http://projectmallard.org/1.0/"
      type="topic" id="firmware-update">
  <info>
    <link type="guide" xref="index#printer"/>
    <title type="sort">3</title>
    <desc>Send a printer a new firmware file, over the network or USB.</desc>
  </info>

  <title>Update a printer's firmware</title>

  <p><guiseq><gui>Printer</gui><gui>Firmware Update…</gui></guiseq> shows the
  firmware the printer runs now and sends it a new firmware file.</p>

  <section id="connection">
    <title>Choose the connection</title>
    <terms>
      <item>
        <title><gui>Network</gui></title>
        <p>Sends to this session's printer.</p>
      </item>
      <item>
        <title><gui>USB</gui></title>
        <p>Lists every USB printer this computer can see, by the name the
        printer gives itself. Its <file>/dev/usb/lpN</file> number can change
        when a printer restarts or is plugged in again, so
        <gui>Refresh</gui> lists them again.</p>
      </item>
    </terms>
  </section>

  <section id="file">
    <title>Choose the file</title>
    <p>Zebra ships firmware as a <file>.zip</file>. Unpack it and choose the
    <file>.zpl</file> file inside, such as <file>V75.20.21Z.zpl</file>. It is
    sent exactly as it is.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="refused">
    <title>If the printer refuses the file</title>
    <p>The printer checks the file as it arrives, and shows
    <gui>Download failed</gui> on its own display if it will not take it.
    LinuxZPL cannot see that, and goes on sending to the end. Put the printer
    in Forced Download Mode and send the file again:</p>
    <steps>
      <item><p>Switch the printer off.</p></item>
      <item><p>Hold the top two menu buttons (ZT410, ZT420) or all three
      (ZT411, ZT421). Other models differ; Zebra's support site has each
      one's.</p></item>
      <item><p>Switch it on, still holding them, until the display shows
      <gui>Download New Firmware</gui> and <gui>USB: Active</gui>.</p></item>
      <item><p>Press <gui>Refresh</gui>, choose the printer's USB entry, and
      press <gui>Update</gui>. The current firmware may show as unavailable
      in this mode; that does not stop the update.</p></item>
    </steps>
    <note>
      <p>The printer's network is off in Forced Download Mode, so it has to
      be USB.</p>
    </note>
  </section>

  <section id="after">
    <title>While it updates</title>
    <p>Once the printer has the whole file it flashes it and restarts by
    itself.</p>
    <note style="warning">
      <p>Do not switch the printer off before it has restarted.</p>
    </note>
  </section>

  <section id="permission">
    <title>No permission to open a USB printer</title>
    <p>Add yourself to the group the message names (usually
    <sys>lp</sys>), then log out and back in.</p>
  </section>
</page>
